A steaming ceramic cup of café latte sits on a worn marble café table in late afternoon golden light, the milk foam swirling in elegant patterns on the surface. Behind it, through a rain-spotted window, the hazy silhouette of Singapore's shophouse architecture blends with modern high-rises. A small potted orchid and scattered Singapore dollar coins rest beside the cup. The scene is rendered in Vincent van Gogh's expressive post-impressionist style with bold, swirling brushstrokes in warm ochres, creamy whites, and deep coffee browns, thick impasto texture creating movement in the steam rising from the cup, the background alive with characteristic undulating energy and visible directional brushwork.
